; A bare `any` type-choice arm in LAST position (`tstr / any`) is a SUPPORTED construct: the arm
; lowers to the AnyCbor runtime type and dispatches via forced backtracking (a typed arm
; matching on wire type but failing on content falls through to the `any` catch-all).
; Full-surface (the wasm AnyCbor wrapper exists), so this row is `ok` under this catalog's default
; `--wasm=true` profile. The rust-only (`--wasm=false`) support is pinned by the `any_positions_*`
; whole_program snapshots and the `tests/any-choice` content-fallthrough integration fixture; the
; wasm surface by the `any-choice` corpus row of `wasm_api_parity`. DISTINCT from the NON-LAST
; rejection (`any / tstr`, tests/robustness/choice_any_arm.cddl).
a = tstr / any
